ch carries the exact eventKind that was written.\n+  const replayEvents: MessageEventInput[] = eventsUpToFork.map(\n+    (record) =>\n+      ({\n+        eventKind: record.eventKind,\n+        idempotencyKey: record.idempotencyKey,\n+        actor: record.actor,\n+        harness: record.harness,\n+        payload: record.payload,\n+      }) as MessageEventInput,\n+  );\n+\n+  // Replay through the normal intake path into the target thread.\n+  // This uses the same capture converter path, preserving all semantics.\n+  const result = await instance.sdk.intakeStream.messageEvents(target, replayEvents);\n+  if (!result.ok) {\n+    return {\n+      ok: false,\n+      error: {\n+        errorClass: result.error.errorClass,\n+        code: result.error.code,\n+        reason: `fork replay failed: ${result.error.reason}`,\n+      },\n+    };\n+  }\n+\n+  return { ok: true, value: undefined };\n }\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"agent_message","text":"Fixed all 4 verifier blockers in the allowed files.\n\nChanged:\n- Fork routing now depends on `session_before_fork` hook data, not `event.reason`; TC-3.1 now exercises `reason: \"startup\"`.\n- PI session-tree fallback now reads real session tree entry IDs from `ctx.sessionManager.getEntries()` and falls back to `previousSessionFile` JSONL.\n- Seed failure now fails closed: records `fork_seed_failed`, disposes the target instance, clears capture state, and returns instead of continuing with an empty fork.\n- TC-3.3 now asserts source ready forms versus target pending queued forms before drain, proving requeue rather than copied ready forms.\n\nGate passed:\n\n`pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify`\n\nResult: 16 test files passed, 82 tests passed."}}
